%[text] # 오픈 루프 데이터 생성
%[text] ## ※ 하드웨어 보유한 경우에만 수행. 
%[text] ## Preparation
%[text] Run the Simulink model [Bicopter\_OpenLoop.slx](file:Bicopter_OpenLoop.)**,** and navigate to hardware settings.
%[text] ![hardware\_settings\_sc.png](text:image:902a)
%[text] Under the settings, navigate to **Wi-Fi Properties** and enter your network credentials. If your network requires additional authentication, consider using a different network, or a personal hotspot. Ensure that your computer is connected to the same network.
%[text] ![wifi\_settings.png](text:image:3c39)
%[text] With the Arduino connected to your computer via USB, click **Build, Deploy & Start** under the **Hardware** tab.
%[text] ![build\_deploy\_start.png](text:image:337b)
%[text] Next turn the motor driver on, and disconnect the USB cable. After programming, locate the IP address of the Arduino in the output displayed in the **Diagnostic Viewer**.
%[text] ![IP\_address.png](text:image:682e)
clear
close all
IPADRR='10.179.103.135' % 필요에 맞게 IP 주소 수정 하세요.
%%
%[text] ## Open Loop Test
%[text] To carry out the open-loop test, disconnect the USB cable from the device, and flip the power switch to that the device green LED is on (battery operation). At this point the program have been loaded in the Arduino. 
%[text]  The input test data can be generated using the MATLAB function idinput() as follows:
dur=6000; % number of data points
Input = idinput(dur, 'rbs', [0 0.1], [-20 20]);
%[text] This generates a binary input with a frequency bandwidth from 0 to 0.1 of the Nyquist frequency and a range from -20 to 20. Once data has been generated, run the following script to send it to the Arduino and collect response. **Make sure to** **keep clear from the propellers before running the following sequence!!!**
tcp = tcpclient(IPADRR,25000);
write(tcp,0,"int8");
pause(1);
write(tcp,Input,'int8');
flush(tcp);
tic
en = 0;
while en == 0
    dat = read(tcp,2,'double');
    en = dat(2);
end
D = read(tcp,2*dur,'double');
Output = D(1:2:end);
en = D(2:2:end);
T_f = toc;
clear tcp
ts = 0.01;
data = iddata(Output',Input,'Ts',ts); % Save data and plot it
close all; 
plot(data)
